---
import ServiceSection from "../components/ServiceSection.astro";
import Endpoint from "../components/Endpoint.astro";
import RustSchema from "../components/RustSchema.astro";
---

<ServiceSection id="service-s2multiplayer">
  <Fragment slot="title"><code>S2Mp</code> — SC2 multiplayer and groups</Fragment>
<p>Slot 13 carries both the <code>S2Map</code> namespace and the Battle.net group
    subsystem. Blizzard also calls a group a “club.” The service lists and searches
    groups, reads group data, answers invitations, subscribes to game-group data,
    and reads map favorites.</p>
    <p>Some decoders are <em>positional</em>. A positional decoder uses absolute bit
    offsets from the start of the record. The offsets include the route header.
    Generated order can add reserved bits beyond the metadata fields.</p>
    <p class="endpoint-index">
      <a href="#s2map-game-groups">S2Map/11 and S2Map/12</a><a href="#s2map-favorites">S2Map/13 favorites</a>
      <a href="#s2multiplayer-get-toon-clubs">S2Mp/46 GetToonClubs</a><a href="#s2multiplayer-get-toon-clubs-response">S2Mp/46 response</a>
      <a href="#s2multiplayer-club-subscribe">S2Mp/47 ClubSubscribe</a><a href="#s2multiplayer-club-change">S2Mp/49 ClubChange</a>
      <a href="#s2multiplayer-search-clubs">S2Mp/51 SearchClubs</a><a href="#s2multiplayer-search-clubs-response">S2Mp/51 response</a>
      <a href="#s2multiplayer-member-clan-tags">S2Mp/53 MemberClanTags</a><a href="#s2multiplayer-invite-action">S2Mp/54 InviteAction</a>
      <a href="#s2multiplayer-get-club-info">S2Mp/55 GetClubInfo</a><a href="#s2multiplayer-get-club-info-response">S2Mp/55 response</a>
      <a href="#s2multiplayer-club-settings">S2Mp/57 ClubSettings</a>
    </p>

    <Endpoint id="s2map-game-groups" direction="bidirectional" phase="protected bootstrap" structure="generated order" status="capture decoded">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>S2Map/11</code> GameGroupSubscribe and <code>S2Map/12</code> GameGroupUpdate</Fragment>
      <p>Subscribes to a tagged game- or map-group feed. The server returns paged
      updates whose result choice contains either map short links or map-group IDs.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`// client → server, command 11
struct GameGroupSubscribeRequest {
    tag: FourCC,
    group_type: bool,
}

// server → client, command 12
struct GameGroupUpdate {
    generated_prefix: Bits<5>,
    is_last: bool,
    generated_marker: Bits<28>,
    tag: FourCC,
    is_first: bool,
    results: GameGroupResults,
}

enum GameGroupResults {
    GameGroup(Vec<S2MapShortLink>),
    MapGroup(Vec<u32>),
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">The observed generated marker is
      <code>0x00d5cc00</code>. A different marker identifies an unknown build
      layout and must halt decoding.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="s2map-favorites" direction="bidirectional" phase="protected bootstrap" structure="generated order" status="capture decoded">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>S2Map/13</code> S2ListMapFavorites</Fragment>
      <p>Requests favorites for the active or explicitly named toon and returns a
      page of map links.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`// client → server
struct ListMapFavoritesRequest {
    toon: Option<ToonFullName>,
}

// server → client
struct ListMapFavoritesResponse {
    result: Result<FavoritesPage, u16>,
}

struct FavoritesPage {
    favorites: Vec<MapFavorite>,
    end_of_list: bool,
    external_profile: bool,
}`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="s2multiplayer-get-toon-clubs" direction="client → server" phase="protected" structure="logical order" status="live verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>S2Mp/46</code> Club::GetToonClubs</Fragment>
      <p>Asks which groups a toon belongs to. The answer returns on the same
      command id.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct GetToonClubsRequest {
    token: u32,
    handle: ToonHandle,
}

struct ToonHandle {
    program_id: u32,
    region: u8,
    realm: u32,
    id: u64,
}

// 168 payload bits; 23-byte record after final alignment`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="s2multiplayer-get-toon-clubs-response" direction="server → client" phase="protected" structure="positional (generated order)" status="capture verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>S2Mp/46</code> Club::GetToonClubsResponse</Fragment>
      <p>Contains a <code>ClubSummaryInfo</code> array for the account. The element
      layout is also used by <code>S2Mp/55</code>. Each offset is relative to the
      element start <code>S</code>.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct GetToonClubsResponse {
    result_tag: bool, // bit 11; false means success
    club_count: u8,  // bits 12..20, 0..=201
    token: u32,
    clubs: Vec<ClubSummaryInfo>, // exactly club_count elements
    tail: u32,
    rank_count: u8,
    ranks: Vec<u8>, // one rank for each club
    is_last_packet: bool,
}

struct ClubSummaryInfo {
    internal_id: u32,       // S + 0 bits
    club_id: u32,           // S + 32; the ID Battle.net shows
    category: u8,           // S + 64
    name: String,           // u8 byte count, 0..=32; then byte-align
    private: bool,          // name_end + 128
    kind: u8,               // name_end + 134
    tag: Option<String>,    // flag at name_end + 206; u5 length, 0..=24
    icon: Option<[u8; 40]>, // flag at cursor + 28; then byte-align
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">Start positional decoding at bit 0 of the record.
      The name length is an eight-bit count. The maximum name length is 32 bytes.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="s2multiplayer-club-subscribe" direction="client → server" phase="protected bootstrap" structure="generated order" status="capture verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>S2Mp/47</code> Club::ClubSubscribeRequest</Fragment>
      <p>Subscribes to one or more club event streams. Each subscription names the
      club, the event class, and the last event stamp already held by the client.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`record ClubSubscribeRecord {
    command_id: u6 = 47,
    service_present: u1 = 1,
    service_slot: u4 = 13,
    payload: ClubSubscribeRequest,
    final_alignment: byte,
}

struct ClubSubscribeRequest {
    subscriptions: SubscriptionList,
}

type SubscriptionList = Array<SubscriptionSyncInfo> {
    count_bits: 8,
    count_range: 0..=200,
}

struct SubscriptionSyncInfo {
    filler_before_stamp: Reserved<11>,
    stamp: i32,
    club_id: u32,
    type: u3,
}`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="s2multiplayer-club-change" direction="server → client" phase="protected" structure="generated order" status="capture verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>S2Mp/49</code> Club::ClubChangeNotification</Fragment>
      <p>Delivers subscribed club changes. The change kind selects summary,
      membership, status, announcement, event, description, or message-board data.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`record ClubChangeRecord {
    command_id: u6 = 49,
    service_present: u1 = 1,
    service_slot: u4 = 13,
    payload: ClubChangeNotification,
    final_alignment: byte,
}

struct ClubChangeNotification {
    deltas: ClubChangeInfoList,
}`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="s2multiplayer-search-clubs" direction="client → server" phase="protected" structure="generated order" status="defined">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>S2Mp/51</code> Club::SearchClubs</Fragment>
      <p>Searches Battle.net groups by name. The type filter excludes clans so the
      results are joinable communities.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct SearchClubsRequest {
    token: u32,
    search: ClubSearch,
}

enum ClubSearch {
    Name {
        name: String,
        club_type: u32, // 1 = group
        category: u32,  // 0 = any
        locale: FourCC, // 0
    },
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">The embedded BSN metadata supplies the field widths.
      This record is sent when the user starts a group search. The current request
      uses token <code>0</code>.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="s2multiplayer-search-clubs-response" direction="server → client" phase="protected" structure="reflected order" status="metadata decoded">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>S2Mp/51</code> Club::SearchClubsResponse</Fragment>
      <p>Returns the matching group IDs. Fetch names and member counts through the
      corresponding group-info endpoints.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct SearchClubsResponse {
    token: u32,
    result: SearchResult,
}

enum SearchResult {
    Matches(Vec<u32>), // club IDs
    Failure,
}`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="s2multiplayer-member-clan-tags" direction="server → client" phase="protected" structure="reflected order" status="metadata decoded">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>S2Mp/53</code> Club::GetMemberClanTagsResponse</Fragment>
      <p>Returns clan tags for members. Retail roster state obtains each member's
      clan tag from presence field <code>0x50004</code>.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct GetMemberClanTagsResponse {
    token: u32,
    result: u16,
    club_id: Option<u32>,
    club_tag: Option<String>,
}`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="s2multiplayer-invite-action" direction="bidirectional" phase="protected" structure="positional (generated order)" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>S2Mp/54</code> Club::InviteAction</Fragment>
      <p>Carries a group or clan invitation (<code>code 0</code>) and its
      accept / decline / auto-decline answer (<code>codes 1 / 2 / 3</code>). The
      record is a fixed 208-bit positional layout.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct InviteAction {
    action: InviteActionCode, // bits 11..13: invited, accepted, declined, auto-declined
    member: InviteMember,
    club_id: u32,             // bits 149..181
    _reserved: Reserved<11>, // bits 181..192; value 4
    result: u16,              // bits 192..208
}

struct InviteMember {
    program_id: u32, // bits 13..45
    kind: u8,        // bits 45..53
    realm: u32,      // bits 53..85
    toon_id: u64,    // bits 85..149
}`} />
      <p class="endpoint-note">An answer carries an empty member handle (program id
      only); only an invitation (code 0) names the invitee. The reader takes the
      program id at bit 13 and the club id at bit 149, then seeks to bit 208.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="s2multiplayer-get-club-info" direction="client → server" phase="protected" structure="generated order" status="verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>S2Mp/55</code> Club::GetClubInfo</Fragment>
      <p>Fetches name and tag for group ids an invitation carried only by number.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct GetClubInfoRequest {
    token: u32,
    clubs: Vec<u32>, // club IDs
}`} />
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="s2multiplayer-get-club-info-response" direction="server → client" phase="protected" structure="positional (generated order)" status="capture verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>S2Mp/55</code> Club::GetClubInfoResponse</Fragment>
      <p>The same <code>ClubSummaryInfo</code> element walk as <code>S2Mp/46</code>,
      for the requested ids. Its tail is shorter: past the last element it carries
      <code>isLastPacket</code> and a zero-length rank list.</p>
    </Endpoint>

    <Endpoint id="s2multiplayer-club-settings" direction="server → client" phase="protected bootstrap" structure="generated order" status="boundary verified">
      <Fragment slot="title"><code>S2Mp/57</code> Club::ClubSettings</Fragment>
      <p>Supplies club-name and tag validation expressions plus cache size and expiry
      policy.</p>
      <RustSchema code={`struct ClubSettings {
    name_pattern: String, // byte count: 13 wire bits, 0..=4096
    tag_pattern: String,  // byte count: 13 wire bits, 0..=4096
    information_cache_size: u32,
    member_cache_size: u32,
    information_expiry: i32,
    online_status_expiry: i32,
    event_expiry: i32,
}`} />
    </Endpoint>
</ServiceSection>
